{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790303429,"nonce":"MnOu73c5oM5rtuplN5BqOxXyaPo=","title":"Reported on IRC (#kernel.org / b4), 2026-09-25:","message":"07:31 \u003cbroonie\u003e mricon: Does b4 store agent reviews in git objects separate to the branches? I'm getting some complaints that \"the stored git blob is missing\" after having moved reviews to a different machine.\n16:09 \u003cmricon\u003e Not agent reviews, but cached mbox data and some other stuff. It stores them as loose blobs and they should be recreated on the fly when found missing. So it should be just an info level message.\n16:40 \u003cbroonie\u003e Ah, I think this was codex having figured out that they shold be there and trying to read them directly.\n17:35 \u003cmricon\u003e Yes, agents are instructed to check for them.\n17:36 \u003cmricon\u003e To give more review context for things like \"has issue X raised by reviewer Y in v1 been addressed?\"\n17:37 \u003cbroonie\u003e I see. Might be worth having something to regenerate them for the moving machines use case.\n21:36 \u003cmricon\u003e I think running \"u\" update fills those back if it finds them missing, but I need to verify that.\n\nVerification (see RCA below): \"u\" does NOT reliably refill them.","files":null}]}